{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>And I said: I am doomed.</b> I am cut off from being among the company of the holy ones, like ודמיתי אמך (Hosea 4:5). And some say from the root דמי (Psalms 62:6); this too is correct:" "The reason for <b>a man of impure lips.</b> In my opinion, the prophet grew up among Israel, who were impure in deed and in speech, and so he learned from their speech — and the proof is ויסרני מלכת בדרך העם הזה (Isaiah 8:11). Therefore he said, 'and among a people of impure lips I dwell.'" "And the reason for <b>for my eyes have seen the King, YHWH of Hosts</b> — that He is holy, and I feared to declare His holiness on account of the impurity of my lips. And even though he said 'my eyes have seen,' he saw this in visions of prophecy."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:52:10.156237724Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}